Chapter: SkillCurve
  cites Uoaix chapter Skill1998

 NPC economy actors only (players gain by skc-learn below). Gain (Damian, 2026-10-06): skill is the log of
 uses, so the uses per 0.1 grow exponentially, 10 * 80^(level/1000): 10 at 0.0
 and 800 at 100.0, for every character alike. skc-root is 80^(1/1000) at the
 2^20 fixed point, rounded. Below 50.0 a failure gains a normal gain; from
 50.0 a failure gains a tenth of one, and a success gains fully on a
 difficulty within 10.0 of the level or above, falling to nothing 20.0 below
 (Skill_Experience's gain radius). Success bonus (Damian, 2026-10-06): a success
 gains skc-bonus tenths of that: 10x below 50.0, tapering linearly to 1x at
 100.0, which takes one fisher from 0.0 to 50.0 in 4,215 uses, inside the
 4,800 a 3 s cooldown allows in 4 hours.

  skc-root : Integer = 1053181
  skc-bonus : Integer -> Integer
  skc-bonus (level) = if level < 500 then 100 else 100 - 90 * (min 1000 level - 500) / 500
  skc-pow : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  skc-pow (base) (n) (acc) = if n == 0 then acc
    else skc-pow (base * base / 1048576) (n / 2) (if int-mod n 2 == 1 then acc * base / 1048576 else acc)
  skc-uses : Integer -> Integer
  skc-uses (level) = (10 * skc-pow skc-root (max 0 (min 1000 level)) 1048576 + 524288) / 1048576
  skc-gain-at : Integer, Integer, Integer, Boolean -> Integer
  skc-gain-at (rate) (level) (difficulty) (success) = let base = min 1000 (rate * 10 / skc-uses level)
    in let full = if success then min 1000 (base * skc-bonus level / 10) else base
    in if difficulty + 200 < level then 0
    else if level < 500 then full
    else if not success then base / 10
    else if difficulty + 100 >= level then full
    else full * (difficulty + 200 - level) / 100
 A play gain of 0.1 on a character's 46 skill cells, to 100.0 a skill. No total cap and no decay (Damian, 2026-10-12,
 D7: "no skill caps, no decay"). 1 when the skill rose.
  skc-total-cells : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  skc-total-cells (cells) (i) = if i == 46 then 0 else peek-qword cells (i * 8) + skc-total-cells cells (i + 1)
  skc-train : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  skc-train (cells) (skill) (draw) = if cells == 0 | skill < 0 | skill >= 46 then 0
    else let level = peek-qword cells (skill * 8)
    in if level >= 1000 then 0
    else let raised = poke-qword cells (skill * 8) (level + 1) in 1
 A practised check on a character's skill row: the 1998 gain (Skill1998) for a check whose success chance was chance,
 raised a tenth at a time under the total. card 0 checks the bare skill. The tenths raised.
  skc-check-chance : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  skc-check-chance (cells) (card) (skill) (difficulty) (range) = if cells == 0 | skill < 0 | skill >= 46 then 0
    else let base = peek-qword cells (skill * 8)
    in let value = if card == 0 then base else s98-value skill base (skc-stat card 0) (skc-stat card 1) (skc-stat card 2)
    in s98-chance value difficulty range
  skc-learn : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Boolean, Integer -> Integer
  skc-learn (cells) (card) (skill) (chance) (passed) (draw) = skc-learn-at cells card skill chance passed 100 draw
  skc-learn-at : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Boolean, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  skc-learn-at (cells) (card) (skill) (chance) (passed) (percent) (draw) = if cells == 0 | skill < 0 | skill >= 46 then 0
    else let base = peek-qword cells (skill * 8)
    in let stat = skc-stat-try card skill base percent draw
    in if not (s98-learns base passed False) then 0
    else skc-raise cells card skill (s98-tenths (s98-gain skill base chance percent) (int-mod (bit-and draw #7FFFFFFF) 1000)) draw 0
  skc-raise : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  skc-raise (cells) (card) (skill) (left) (draw) (raised) = if left <= 0 then raised
    else if skc-train cells skill (draw + left) == 0 then raised
    else skc-raise cells card skill (left - 1) draw (raised + 1)
 1998 stat gain (OUO skill.c CMobile_TryStatGain, 0x004D5A5D; CalcStatThreshold, 0x004D5A2C): a try rolls strength,
 dexterity and intelligence once each, and raises a stat by 1 when (100 - stat) * weight * value / 1000 beats a roll of 0 to
 19999, weight the skill's percent for that stat in skills.txt (all three judged on the stats before the try). A stat
 at 100 ends the raises of it and of every stat after it in that try. A check (SkillCheck, 0x004D52ED, divisor 1) tries
 at value CalcDelay * gain percent / 10000; a direct use at half its gain factor. A stat stops at 100 (Damian,
 2026-10-07, CompositeSkillCommand) and the three at 225 (ServUO StatCap, UOAIX's; 1998 has none). The character record
 holds a raised stat at byte 147 + stat over its creation stat at 79 + stat.
  skc-stat : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  skc-stat (card) (stat) = let set = peek-byte card (147 + stat) in if set > 0 then set else peek-byte card (79 + stat)
  skc-next : Integer -> Integer
  skc-next (x) = int-mod (bit-and x #FFFFFFFF * 1664525 + 1013904223) 4294967296
  skc-stat-weight : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  skc-stat-weight (skill) (stat) = if stat == 0 then list-at s98d-str skill else if stat == 1 then list-at s98d-dex skill else list-at s98d-int skill
  skc-stat-beats : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  skc-stat-beats (card) (skill) (value) (stat) (x) = (100 - skc-stat card stat) * skc-stat-weight skill stat * value / 1000 > int-mod (bit-shru x 8) 20000
  skc-stat-flag : Integer, Integer, Boolean, Integer -> Integer
  skc-stat-flag (card) (stat) (won) (flag) = if won & skc-stat card stat + flag > 100 then 0 else flag
  skc-stat-room : Integer -> Boolean
  skc-stat-room (card) = skc-stat card 0 + skc-stat card 1 + skc-stat card 2 < 225
  skc-stat-raise : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  skc-stat-raise (card) (stat) = let raised = poke-byte card (147 + stat) (skc-stat card stat + 1) in stat
 A try at value; the lowest stat raised (0 to 2), or -1.
  skc-stat-value : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  skc-stat-value (card) (skill) (value) (draw) = if card == 0 | not (s98-valid skill) | value <= 0 then -1
    else let x0 = skc-next draw
    in let x1 = skc-next x0
    in let x2 = skc-next x1
    in let w0 = skc-stat-beats card skill value 0 x0
    in let w1 = skc-stat-beats card skill value 1 x1
    in let w2 = skc-stat-beats card skill value 2 x2
    in let f0 = skc-stat-flag card 0 w0 1
    in let r0 = if w0 & f0 == 1 & skc-stat-room card then skc-stat-raise card 0 else -1
    in let f1 = skc-stat-flag card 1 w1 f0
    in let r1 = if w1 & f1 == 1 & skc-stat-room card then skc-stat-raise card 1 else -1
    in let f2 = skc-stat-flag card 2 w2 f1
    in let r2 = if w2 & f2 == 1 & skc-stat-room card then skc-stat-raise card 2 else -1
    in if r0 >= 0 then r0 else if r1 >= 0 then r1 else r2
 A check's try, on the skill's base and the check's gain percent.
  skc-stat-try : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  skc-stat-try (card) (skill) (base) (percent) (draw) = if card == 0 | not (s98-valid skill) then -1
    else skc-stat-value card skill (s98-delay skill base * percent / 10000) draw
 A successful direct use's try: gain factor 100, so value 50.
  skc-stat-gain : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  skc-stat-gain (card) (skill) (draw) = skc-stat-value card skill 50 draw

